{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_hjchz2lciniqfuwlqiig73qzr7qmk4blqfacmgqtixa74lktltrq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. The translation is complete and verified.\n\n## Scope enumerated first\nThe C build (`CMakeLists.txt`) globs all three `.c` files into one shared library. `nm -D` on the C `.so` gives exactly **10 exported symbols** — no namespace-renaming macros are present in the headers, so source names are the final linker names:\n\n| Source | Symbols |\n|---|---|\n| `logger.c` | `initialize_logger`, `log_info`, `log_warning`, `log_error`, `finalize_logger` |\n| `task_manager.c` | `create_task_manager`, `add_task`, `print_tasks`, `destroy_task_manager` |\n| `driver.c` | `driver` |\n\n## Completion gate — PASSED\n`diff` of the two `nm -D` lists is **empty**: 10 C exports, 10 Rust exports, same names, same `T` binding, no extras.\n\n## Files written (`translation/`)\n- `Cargo.toml` — `crate-type = [\"cdylib\"]`\n- `src/cstd.rs`, `src/logger.rs`, `src/task_manager.rs`, `src/driver.rs`, `src/lib.rs`\n\n## Key fidelity decisions\n- **Output goes through the same libc stdio** (`printf`/`fprintf`/`fopen`/`fclose`), not Rust's `std::io`. This preserves buffering, `%d`/`%s` formatting, and glibc's `(null)` rendering for a null `%s`. Likewise `malloc`/`free`/`getenv`/`atoi`/`strchr`/`strlen`/`strncpy` are the real libc ones, so `atoi` edge cases and heap pointer compatibility with C `free` match exactly.\n- **Bugs preserved, not fixed**: `finalize_logger` `fclose`s but never nulls `log_file` (dangling pointer on re-use); `add_task`/`print_tasks`/`destroy_task_manager` don't null-check `manager`; `initialize_logger` overwrites a live `log_file` handle without closing it.\n- `max_tasks * sizeof(Task)` reproduces C's `int`→`size_t` sign-extension and mod-2⁶⁴ wraparound, so a negative `MAX_TASKS` yields a huge size, `malloc` fails, and you get the `\"Failed to allocate memory for tasks.\"` path — verified identical.\n- `#[repr(C)]` structs verified as 260 / 16 bytes, matching C.\n\n## Verification\nBuilt a `dlopen` harness exercising the whole ABI (not just `driver`) and ran **103 differential cases** comparing return code, stdout, stderr, and every file created (byte-for-byte): input splitting edge cases (empty, leading/trailing/consecutive newlines, CRLF, 254/255/256/257-byte tasks, printf specifiers in data, UTF-8, 1000 tasks), a 24-value `MAX_TASKS` sweep, a `LOG_FILE` sweep including unwritable paths, the logger called before `initialize_logger`, and `print_tasks` on a caller-built `TaskManager`. **103/103 identical.**\n\nOne thing worth flagging: my first test script had a latent bug — unset env vars were being passed as `LOG_FILE=\"\"`, which made `fopen(\"\")` fail, so *every* case silently took the logger-failure path and the log-file comparison globbed nothing. Both libraries agreed, so it still \"passed\" while testing almost nothing. I rewrote it in Python with proper env handling, then added a **negative control**: a two-line mutation of the C source (`priority` starting at 0, `[INFO]`→`[info]`) triggers 92/103 failures, confirming the suite actually discriminates. The scratch test directory has been removed; `c_src/` is unmodified."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2894,"cache_read_input_tokens":54619,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2894,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"84094a79-c9f9-4eae-8abd-5a6be448b59c","uuid":"ec7723ae-e310-4b59-be28-45692428f484","timestamp":"2026-08-28T06:03:52.672Z"}
